-- title:
--   1/j lies in no minimal prime over varpi in the pole chart
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a principal ideal domain (a commutative domain all of whose ideals are principal), let $K_0$ be a field that is a fraction field of $R$, and let $F$ be a field equipped with compatible $R$- and $K_0$-algebra structures (an $R$-algebra tower through $K_0$). Let $j \in F$ be nonzero, assumed transcendental over $R$, and assume that $F$ is finite-dimensional and separable over the intermediate field $K_0(j)$ obtained by adjoining $j$ to $K_0$ inside $F$. Let $\varpi \in R$ be a prime element. Consider the subalgebra $\mathrm{chartAlgInf}(R,F,j) =$ `chartAlgInf R F j` of $F$ consisting of all elements of $F$ that are integral over the $R$-subalgebra $R[j^{-1}]$ generated by $j^{-1}$, that is, the integral closure of $R[j^{-1}]$ in $F$; inside it, `jInvChartInf R F j` denotes the element $j^{-1}$. The assertion is that for every prime $Q$ that is a minimal prime over the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$ in this ring, one has $j^{-1} \notin Q$.
--
--   Geometrically: no irreducible component of the fibre over the prime $(\varpi)$ of the two-chart integral model attached to $j$ is contained in the locus $j^{-1}=0$, so every such component has its generic point in the chart where $j$ is finite. It is used in the comparison of special fibres of Hecke degeneracy maps on models of modular curves, and in a criterion for localisation-wise membership statements on the two charts.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_jInvChartInf_not_mem_of_mem_minimalPrimes_span.lean

